      "created_at": "2018-05-22T22:41:21Z",
      "updated_at": "2018-05-22T22:41:21Z",
      "body": "1. From the Form Runner home page, admins ask for a given `app/form` to be re-encrypted (for now we won't support re-encrypting `app/*` or `*/*`).\r\n2. Based on the `app/form`, the persistence proxy dispatches the request to the appropriate implementation of the persistence API. Out-of-the-box, for now, we'll implement this only in the relational implementation of the API.\r\n3. The implementation queries the data table to find all the versions of the `app/form` for which we have data. It then iterates over the `app/form/version`.\r\n4. For a given `app/form/version`, it retrieves the form definition, iterates over the corresponding data, and for each runs `FieldEncryption.encryptDataIfNecessary()`, and writes back the result.",
      "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
      "pin": null,
      "reactions": {
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/orbeon/orbeon-forms/issues/comments/391163525/reactions",
